cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this lab in research, courseware, or talks, please cite it as below."
title: "home-lab-siem — reproducible Wazuh + Suricata + Sysmon + MISP SOC stack"
authors:
  - family-names: Zahidi
    given-names: Yassir
    email: yassirzahidi8@gmail.com
type: software
abstract: >-
  A reproducible SOC-grade home lab packaged as docker compose. Wazuh manager
  with custom decoders, Suricata IDS on a span port, Sysmon/auditd telemetry,
  MISP threat intelligence with CIRCL and abuse.ch feeds, and VirusTotal
  enrichment. Mirrors the architecture deployed at the Préfecture de Tétouan
  (SSIC) repackaged so anyone can `docker compose up`.
keywords:
  - siem
  - wazuh
  - suricata
  - sysmon
  - misp
  - blue-team
  - detection-engineering
  - threat-intelligence
  - mitre-attack
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/y-zahidi/home-lab-siem"
url: "https://y-zahidi.github.io"
